[34.445717,"o","\u001b[48;5;238m\u001b[2;1H  - Increased total eosinophil count (HP:0001880)\u001b[84X\r\n  - Recurrent Staphylococcus aureus infections (HP:0002726)\u001b[74X\r\n  - Decreased neutrophil oxidative burst (HP:0003203)\u001b[80X\r\n  - Increased circulating IgE concentration (HP:0003212)\u001b[77X\r\n  - Recurrent pneumonia (HP:0006532)\u001b[97X\r\n  - Prominent forehead (HP:0011220)\u001b[98X\r\n  - Pulmonary pneumatocele (HP:0025419)\u001b[94X\r\n  - Cutaneous abscess (HP:0031292)\u001b[99X\r\n  - Abnormal CD4+ T cell subset proportion (HP:0031392)\u001b[78X\r\n  - Abnormal CD8+ T cell proportion (HP:0031393)\u001b[85X\u001b[12;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  No excluded features were provided.\u001b[96X\u001b[14;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  Use only the symptoms shown here and the bundled dx-toolkit tools in the current workspace. Do not inspect local case files or\u001b[5X\r\n  other repo files. Do not search for case IDs, runtime helpers, package roots, or alternate tool locations. Do not mention local\u001b[4X\r\n  file names or paths in your visible narration. Begin directly with the diagnosis workflow.\u001b[41X\u001b[18;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[49m\n\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n• \u001b(B\u001b[mUsing the miniOdyssey workflow. I’m loading its instructions first, then I’ll run the phenotype-driven ranking against the symptom\u001b[1X\n\u001b[1K\r  list and synthesize the diagnosis from those tool results.\u001b[22;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r•\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[1mExplored\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[24;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r  └ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[36mRead\u001b[39m SKILL.md (miniOdyssey skill)\u001b[25;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[27;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n• \u001b(B\u001b[mI have the workflow constraints. Next I’m pulling the reasoning and output guidance, then I’ll run the first disease-family query\u001b[2X\r\n  from the phenotype anchors: hyper-IgE, staphylococcal skin/lung infections, pneumatoceles, and impaired oxidative burst.\u001b[11X\u001b[30;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r•\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[1mExplored\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2m\r\n  └ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[36mRead\u001b[39m clinical-reasoning.md\u001b[2m, \u001b(B\u001b[mtool-selection-guide.md\u001b[2m, \u001b(B\u001b[mdemo-output-style.md\u001b[56X\u001b[33;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n• \u001b[7mI’m planning to run a commentary update that focuses on potential medical conditions. The pattern suggests hyper-IgE/primary\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[7X\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mimmunodeficiency, with chronic granulomatous disease as a significant alternative. To ensure thoroughness, I’ll approach this with\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1X\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mfour views in parallel: a full phenotype ranking, a focused rescue pass, a disease-family lookup, and a keyword disease search.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4X\u001b[37;133H\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mThen, I’ll execute the plan to gather detailed information.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[40;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n• \u001b(B\u001b[mThe leading family pattern is hyper-IgE primary immunodeficiency, with chronic granulomatous disease still a serious alternate\u001b[5X\r\n  because of the impaired oxidative burst. I’m checking four independent views now: full phenotype ranking, a focused rescue pass,\u001b[3X\u001b[43;133H\u001b[1K\r  disease-family enumeration, and a disease-first keyword search.\u001b[44;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n•\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[1mRan\u001b(B\u001b[m \u001b[38;5;111mdx-omim\u001b[38;5;189m disease-series\u001b[38;5;103m --\u001b[38;5;217mquery\u001b[38;5;189m \u001b[38;5;151m\"hyper IgE syndrome\"\u001b[38;5;103m --\u001b[38;5;217mlimit\u001b[38;5;189m 50\u001b[