 state, \"The best single diagnosis is\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2X\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mSTAT3-related autosomal dominant hyper-IgE syndrome 1 (Job syndrome; STAT3, OMIM 147060)\" while including other possibilities like\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1X\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mIL6ST and ZNF341. I really want to keep the bullets concise but informative, aiming for four key points without overcrowding the\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3X\u001b[43;133H\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mparagraph.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[44;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[46;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r• \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1mLeading diagnosis\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  The best fit is \u001b[1mSTAT3-related autosomal dominant hyper-IgE syndrome 1\u001b(B\u001b[m (\u001b[1mJob syndrome\u001b(B\u001b[m; \u001b[1mSTAT3\u001b(B\u001b[m, \u001b[1mOMIM 147060\u001b(B\u001b[m), with moderate confidence.\r\n  The overall pattern is the classic “original hyper-IgE syndrome” frame rather than a nonspecific "]
[198.590026,"o","atopic or phagocyte-defect\u001b[8X\u001b[51;133H\u001b[1K\r  presentation.\u001b[52;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[1mWhy it fits\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[54;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  - \u001b[1mEczematoid dermatitis, very high IgE, and eosinophilia\u001b(B\u001b[m form the core immunologic pattern of hyper-IgE syndrome.\u001b[18X\r\n  - \u001b[1mRecurrent Staphylococcus aureus skin abscesses\u001b(B\u001b[m plus \u001b[1mrecurrent pneumonia with pulmonary pneumatoceles\u001b(B\u001b[m are especially\u001b[14X\u001b[57;133H\u001b[1K\r    characteristic of the classic Job-syndrome phenotype.\r\n  - \u001b[1mCoarse facial features and a prominent forehead\u001b(B\u001b[m are important nonimmune clues that push this away from simpler infection-prone\u001b[3X\u001b[59;133H\u001b[1K\r    immunodeficiencies and toward \u001b[1mSTAT3-HIES\u001b(B\u001b[m.\r\n  - The phenotype views repeatedly kept the case inside the \u001b[1mhyper-IgE / STAT3-pathway family\u001b(B\u001b[m, with \u001b[1mSTAT3, IL6ST, DOCK8, and ZNF341\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3X\r\n    all surfacing, which is exactly the family structure expected for this syndrome.\u001b[49X\r\n  - The \u001b[1mdecreased neutrophil oxidative burst\u001b(B\u001b[m is the main discordant clue, but by whole-case fit it is not strong enough to outweigh\u001b[2X\r\n    the far more classic Job-syndrome combination of facies, eczema, staphylococcal abscesses, and pneumatoceles.\u001b[20X\u001b[64;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[1mWhy the runner-up lost\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[66;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[48;5;238m\r\n \u001b[132X\u001b[1m\r\n›\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;5;238m \u001b[2mImplement {feature}\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;5;238m\u001b[112X\r\n \u001b[132X\u001b[49m\u001b[71;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r  gpt-5.4 xhigh · /demo/miniOdyssey\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h\u001b[66;1H\u001b[48;5;238m\u001b[68;2H\u001b[132X\u001b[69;22H\u001b[112X\u001b[70;2H\u001b[132X\u001b[49m\u001b[71;48H\u001b[86X\u001b[69