[216.522804,"o","\u001b[?25l\u001b[2;133H\u001b[1K\r    \u001b[2m  \"query\": \"ZNF341 hyper IgE syndrome facial features\",\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r    … +82 lines (ctrl + t to view transcript)\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4;133H\u001b[1K\r    \u001b[2m  ]\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[5;133H\u001b[1K\r    \u001b[2m}\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[6;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n• \u001b[7mI'm looking into IL6ST variants and their relationship with STAT3, particularly how they can lead to \"original hyper-IgE syndrome.\"\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mI wonder if there's a way to differentiate the cases related to IL6ST, especially since dysmorphic facies could also be involved.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2X\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mIt's interesting to consider the implications of these genetic factors and how they might manifest in different individuals. Let's\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1X\n\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[2m\u001b[7msee what more I can find on this topic!\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[11;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[1m\u001b[2m\u001b[7mEvaluating differential diagnoses\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[13;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mThis seems like a solid plan. The differential includes Chronic Granulomatous Disease (CGD), but I wonder if it’s a more nuanced\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3X\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mclinical picture. Maybe I need to consider IL6ST/ZNF341 either as a separate differential or grouped with others. If I were to rank\u001b(B\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mthem, I think I could go with: 1) DOCK8 deficiency, 2) IL6ST/ZNF341-related hyper-IgE syndrome, and 3) Chronic Granulomatous\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[7X\u001b[17;133H\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mDisease. Overall, this feels coherent.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[18;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[1m\u001b[2m\u001b[7mCrafting concise diagnoses\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[20;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mI'm comparing top diagnoses, including DOCK8 and mentioning Chronic Granulomatous Disease (CGD). I should list genetics,\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[11X\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mparticularly focusing on IL6ST/ZNF341, noting DOCK8 as a potential differential. Maybe I can state, \"The best single diagnosis is\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[2X\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mSTAT3-related autosomal dominant hyper-IgE syndrome 1 (Job syndrome; STAT3, OMIM 147060)\" while including other possibilities like\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1X\r\n  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mIL6ST and ZNF341. I really want to keep the bullets concise but informative, aiming for four key points without overcrowding the\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3X\u001b[25;133H\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[2m\u001b[7mparagraph.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[26;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[28;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r• \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1mLeading diagnosis\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[30;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  The best fit is \u001b[1mSTAT3-related autosomal dominant hyper-IgE syndrome 1\u001b(B\u001b[m (\u001b[1mJob syndrome\u001b(B\u001b[m; \u001b[1mSTAT3\u001b(B\u001b[m, \u001b[1mOMIM 147060\u001b(B\u001b[m), with moderate confidence.\r\n  The overall pattern is the classic “original hyper-IgE syndrome” frame rather than a nonspecific atopic or phagocyte-defect\u001b[8X\u001b[33;133H\u001b[1K\r  presentation.\u001b[34;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[1mWhy it fits\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[36;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  - \u001b[1mEczematoid dermatitis, very high IgE, and eosinophilia\u001b(B\u001b[m form the core immunologic pattern of hyper-IgE syndrome.\u001b[18X\r\n  - \u001b[1mRecurrent Staphylococcus aureus skin abscesses\u001b(B\u001b[m plus \u001b[1mrecurrent pneumonia with pulmonary pneumatoceles\u001b(B\u001b[m are especially\u001b[14X\u001b[39;133H\u001b[1K\r    characteristic of the classic Job-syndrome phenotype.\r\n  - \u001b[1mCoarse facial features and a prominent forehead\u001b(B\u001b[m are important nonimmune clues that push this away from simpler infection-prone\u001b[3X\u001b[41;133H\u001b[1K\r    immunodeficiencies and toward \u001b[1mSTAT3-HIES\u001b(B\u001b[m.\r\n  - The phenotype views repeatedly kept the case inside the \u001b[1mhyper-IgE / STAT3-pathway family\u001b(B\u001b[m, with \u001b[1mSTAT3, IL6ST, DOCK8, and ZNF341\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[3X\r\n    all surfacing, which is exactly the family structure expected for this syndrome.\u001b[49X\r\n  - The \u001b[1mdecreased neutrophil oxidative burst\u001b(B\u001b[m is the main discordant clue, but by whole-case fit it is not strong enough to outweigh\u001b[2X\r\n    the far more classic Job-syndrome combination of facies, eczema, staphylococcal abscesses, and pneumatoceles.\u001b[20X\u001b[46;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[1mWhy the runner-up lost\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;133H\u001b[1K\r\n "]
[216.522938,"o"," The closest runner-up is \u001b[1mDOCK8 deficiency\u001b(B\u001b[m. It stayed high because it also explains eczema, eosinophilia, elevated IgE, recurrent\u001b[3X\r\n  infections, and abnormal T-cell subsets. What moved this case toward \u001b[1mSTAT3-HIES\u001b(B\u001b[m instead was the more classic \u001b[1mJob-syndrome\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[10X\r\n  \u001b[1mmorphology plus pneumatocele pattern\u001b(B\u001b[m; those features are much more characteristic of \u001b[1mSTAT3-type hyper-IgE syndrome\u001b(B\u001b[m than of DOCK8\u001b[3X\r\n  deficiency. The oxidative-burst abnormality kept chronic granulomatous disease alive as a separate alternate, but CGD did not\u001b[6X\u001b[53;133H\u001b[1K\r  explain the full syndrome nearly as well.\u001b[54;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[1mRanked differential\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[56;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  - \u001b[1mDOCK8 deficiency (hyper-IgE syndrome 2)\u001b(B\u001b[m - strong immune overlap, especially with T-cell abnormalities, but weaker fit for\u001b[8X\u001b[58;133H\u001b[1K\r    characteristic facies and pneumatoceles.\r\n  - \u001b[1mIL6ST- or ZNF341-related hyper-IgE syndrome\u001b(B\u001b[m - close \u001b[1mSTAT3-pathway phenocopies\u001b(B\u001b[m that preserve the same overall syndrome frame.\u001b[5X\r\n  - \u001b[1mChronic granulomatous disease (especially NCF2/CYBB/NCF1-related)\u001b(B\u001b[m - explains the oxidative-burst defect, abscesses, and\u001b[10X\r\n    pneumonia, but not the full hyper-IgE facial/pneumatocele pattern.\u001b[63X\u001b[62;133H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\r  \u001b[1mConfidence note\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[64;133H\u001b[1K\r\n  Confidence is \u001b[1mmoderate\u001b(B\u001b[m: the syndrome pattern strongly favors \u001b[1mclassic STAT3-pathway hyper-IgE syndrome\u001b(B\u001b[m, but the oxidative-burst\u001b[5X\r\n  defect keeps \u001b[1mCGD\u001b(B\u001b[m and other \u001b[1mSTAT3-pathway phenocopies\u001b(B\u001b[m relevant until molecular confirmation.\u001b[40X\u001b[67;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[48;5;238m\r\n \u001b[132X\u001b[1m\r\n›\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;5;238m \u001b[2mImplement {feature}\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[48;5;238m\u001b[112X\r\n \u001b[132X\u001b[49m\u001b[71;133H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r  gpt-5.4 xhigh · /demo/miniOdyssey\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[32m\u001b[7m\u001b[1;3H0\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[32m \"current\"──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[5C1 \"✳ Claude Code\"─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[H\u001b[32m──\u001b[129C──┬\u001b[39m──\u001b[130C──\u001b[2;134H\u001b[32m│\u001b[3;134H│\u001b[4;134H│\u001b[5;134H│\u001b[6;134H│\u001b[7;134H│\u001b[8;134H│\u001b[9;134H│\u001b[10;134H│\u001b[11;134H│\u001b[12;134H│\u001b[13;134H│\u001b[14;134H│\u001b[15;134H│\u001b[16;134H│\u001b[17;134H│\u001b[18;134H│\u001b[19;134H│\u001b[20;134H│\u001b[21;134H│\u001b[22;134H│\u001b[23;134H│\u001b[24;134H│\u001b[25;134H│\u001b[26;134H│\u001b[27;134H│\u001b[28;134H│\u001b[29;134H│\u001b[30;134H│\u001b[31;134H│\u001b[32;134H│\u001b[33;134H│\u001b[34;134H│\u001b[35;134H│\u001b[36;134H│\u001b[37;134H│\u001b[38;134H│\u001b[39;134H│\u001b[40;134H│\u001b[41;134H│\u001b[42;134H│\u001b[43;134H│\u001b[44;134H│\u001b[45;134H│\u001b[46;134H│\u001b[47;134H│\u001b[48;134H│\u001b[49;134H│\u001b[50;134H│\u001b[51;134H│\u001b[52;134H│\u001b[53;134H│\u001b[54;134H│\u001b[55;134H│\u001b[56;134H│\u001b[57;134H│\u001b[58;134H│\u001b[59;134H│\u001b[60;134H│\u001b[61;134H│\u001b[62;134H│\u001b[63;134H│\u001b[64;134H│\u001b[65;134H│\u001b[66;134H│\u001b[67;134H│\u001b[68;134H│\u001b[69;134H│\u001b[70;134H│\u001b[71;134H│\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[30m\u001b[42m\r\n[v7demo_ca0:node*                                                                                                                                                                                                                     